      "side": 1,
      "message": "Now that we\u0027re using templates, instead of macros, I think distinct names are no longer necessary:\n- I believe that any of our given invocations can only match one of the templates. (We can\u0027t, e.g., construct a std::function that takes two parameters, from a method that takes no parameters. Nor the other way around.)\n- Hence: we can use a single name, and let the compiler resolve the overloads.\n- And I think using overloading here would fit within the constraints of our style guide: \"Use overloaded functions (including constructors) only if a reader looking at a call site can get a good idea of what is happening without having to first figure out exactly which overload is being called.\"\n\nBut ultimately, I\u0027ll leave the choice of whether or not to use overloading to your judgment.",
