      "side": 1,
      "message": "(continued from PS4)\n\nI don\u0027t think createWifiStatus is necessary for the pair (or tuple) case. Here are a couple of alternatives:\n\n  // We name the type, so that the make_pair template\n  // can deduce the types of the pair\u0027s elements.\n  std::make_pair(WifiStatus{WifiStatusCode::SUCCESS, \"\"}, \u003cvalue\u003e);\n\nor\n\n  // Alternatively, we can explicitly specify the types of the pair.\n  std::pair\u003cWifiStatus, OtherT\u003e{ {WifiStatusCode::SUCCESS, \"\"}, \u003cother-value\u003e );\n\nThat said, the argument above is strictly technical (i.e., I\u0027m identifying what alternatives are possible).\n\nI\u0027ll leave it to your judgment about what\u0027s best stylistically.",
